Task 1: Setting Up Velociraptor for Endpoint Monitoring
Step 1.1: Install Velociraptor
Download and configure Velociraptor on your system:

# Create working directory
mkdir -p ~/endpoint-forensics-lab
cd ~/endpoint-forensics-lab

# Download Velociraptor binary
wget https://github.com/Velocidex/velociraptor/releases/download/v0.7.0/velociraptor-v0.7.0-linux-amd64

# Make executable
chmod +x velociraptor-v0.7.0-linux-amd64
sudo ln -s $(pwd)/velociraptor-v0.7.0-linux-amd64 /usr/local/bin/velociraptor
Step 1.2: Generate Configuration Files
Create server and client configurations:

# Generate server configuration
velociraptor config generate > server.config.yaml

# Generate client configuration
velociraptor --config server.config.yaml config client > client.config.yaml

# Create necessary directories
mkdir -p logs artifacts
Step 1.3: Start Velociraptor Services
Launch the server and client:

# Start server in background
velociraptor --config server.config.yaml frontend -v &

# Wait for server initialization
sleep 10

# Start client
velociraptor --config client.config.yaml client -v &

# Verify both are running
ps aux | grep velociraptor
